# ⚡ MatrixAnalyst Pro: Enterprise Multi-Agent Financial Intelligence Platform

An adaptive, production-grade AI platform engineered to extract, audit, and analyze complex corporate documentation (like 10-K filings, annual reports, and balance sheets) without data context fragmentation.

## 🧠 Why This Was Built (The Engineering Problem)
Standard naive RAG systems rely on character-based chunking that routinely slices financial tables in half, separating numbers from their headers and causing severe LLM hallucinations. This platform resolves that structural breakdown by implementing a markdown-aware multi-agent architecture powered by **LangGraph**.

## 🛠️ Key Architectural Highlights
- **Intent-Based Routing Node:** Dynamically evaluates incoming user queries. Descriptive policy questions are automatically routed to a dense text retrieval node, while arithmetic requests are sent to a forensic calculation module.
- **Data Ingestion Optimization:** Utilizes structural `MarkdownTextSplitter` parameters to safeguard multi-column data borders and keep table rows perfectly whole.
- **Direct Variable Override Gate:** Automatically detects when a user supplies raw numbers manually inside the chat container, completely bypassing vector database lag to execute instant processing logic.
- **Enterprise Security Wrapper:** Protected by a self-contained Department Access authentication gateway wall and modular whitelabel structure configurations.

## 💻 Technical Stack
- **Orchestration:** LangGraph (StateGraph Engine)
- **Framework:** LangChain & Python
- **Vector Database:** FAISS Cluster Index
- **Compute Layer:** Groq LPU Infrastructure (Llama 3.1)
- **Frontend Layer:** Streamlit (Pure-code Micro-SaaS styling overrides)